#AI:1
TYPE="stack_meta"
STACK="gbdk"
DISPLAY_NAME="Game Boy Development Kit (GBDK-2020)"

DESCRIPTION:
C-based Game Boy / Game Boy Color homebrew development. Uses the
GBDK-2020 fork of the original GBDK with SDCC compiler. Targets DMG,
CGB, and (via GBA mode) AGB. Suitable for games, demos, and link-cable
peripherals.

RECOMMENDED_TOOLS:
- Toolchain:     GBDK-2020 (https://github.com/gbdk-2020/gbdk-2020)
- Compiler:      SDCC (bundled with GBDK)
- Build:         GNU make (Makefile drives lcc/SDCC)
- Emulator:      SameBoy (accurate, headless+Lua scriptable) and BGB (debugger, link-cable sim)
- Tile/sprite:   png2asset (bundled), Tiled editor for maps, GBStudio for high-level prototyping
- Source mgmt:   git; .gb ROMs are binary — keep in build/ via .gitignore

INIT_NOTES:
- init-project.sh copies code.ai → .claude/rules/code.ai
- init-project.sh copies tests.ai → .claude/rules/tests.ai
- Install GBDK-2020 to /opt/gbdk or similar, then set GBDK_HOME in Makefile or environment
- Hard ROM-size limits — pick MBC (memory bank controller) early; switching mid-project is painful
- No floating point, no heap (no malloc) — design for static buffers from day one
